  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure will bring continuing tranquil conditions\nthrough Wednesday. \n\nHigh pressure over the area will continue to bring dry and tranquil\nweather for the next few days. For the rest of today and Tuesday,\nmostly sunny skies are expected with highs generally in the mid 70s\nto mid 80s, with Tuesday being a few degrees warmer than today.\nTemps at night will cool off a bit, with lows mainly in the 50s due\nto light winds and clear skies. Right along the coast, the Delaware\nBay, and the Philly metro area it will be a bit warmer with lows in\nthe low 60s. \n\nBy Wednesday, the center of high pressure will shift offshore leading\nto southwest return flow setting up. This will result in a continuing\nwarming trend with conditions also turning a bit more humid as dew\npoints increase. However, it will be partly to mostly sunny with any\nshowers/storms staying well north of the area through the day.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A cold front will cross the area Thursday bringing \nthe potential for a round of showers and storms.\n\nAs the high moves away, it will allow low pressure to the north\nto move by and usher a cold front across our region. The front\nwill tap into some of the heat and humidity to create scattered\nshowers and a few tstms. It's possible that a few of the showers\nmay arrive towards dawn across the southern Poconos and north NJ\nwhere chance POPs are in the fcst. It could end up being a rather\nuneventful FROPA as it may move through during the morning hours\nwhen the heating will be minimized. We'll continue with the chance\nPOPs for the area attm. Mostly morning rains N/W and afternoon S/E.\n\nFollowing the front, cooler and drier air arrives for Friday and\nmuch of the upcoming weekend.",
